Z||000000||NOS3800||07-16-2001||12:06 AM||||I was wondering how many of you there were out there. <BR>Anyway, do you notice a decrease in performance in quarter mile times as your bottle gets past half full? <BR>Also, I noticed I get my best times on NOS in warmer weather. Is this normal or could it just be that the bottle was getting empty?<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||07-16-2001||12:13 AM||||Simple physics.  As your bottle gets empty, or the temp drops, the pressure in the bottle drops, so you're getting less NOS than with a full or warm tank.  That's why they make tank warmers.  Be careful not to over heat them!  Big bang theory in action!||||reg||4
Z||000002||1FST2M6||07-16-2001||09:28 AM||||your suposed to keep the bottle around 80* and the pressure at about 800psi. thats why the bottle warmers aid in keeping your times consistant... unfortunatly the bottle freezes WAY faster then the warmer works. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> you REALLLLLY have to screw somthing up to pop a bottle. a bottle warmer if wired correctly shuts off at 1000psi or 85*  at least mine does. and the guy you've all seen with a laid open maxima.. that was HIS fault... not the nitrous bottles or the manufacturs fault. he wired it straight on. and it HAD to be on for a VERY long time.. a nitrous bottle will pop the saftey valve at 3000psi that WON'T blow up a car.  <P>( Nitrous Express, Wet) <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||07-16-2001||10:44 AM||||Yeah, they're pretty safe.  But I figured I'd throw in that caveat - modern liability being what it is today.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||07-16-2001||10:49 AM||||LOL.. ok.. makes sense...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><BR>street racing is bad.. don't street race.. mmm kay||||reg||1
Z||000005||kempo||07-16-2001||01:17 PM||||What is the best NOS system to use?  I heard that ZEX NOS system is a really good system.  Also, where do you place your bottles, in the trunk, cab, front trunk?  <BR>-Kemp||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||07-16-2001||02:59 PM||||if your running forced induction a dry kit through the s/c or turbo. if your running naturally aspirated Nitrous Express wet kit. i've had NOS (ok) i worked wih zex (ok), Venom (suck), edelbrock (ok) but the NX kit is SOOOO much better than the other kits i've had.  <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||NOS3800||07-16-2001||06:11 PM||||I do not think the ZEX kit will work with the Fiero 2.8's and 2.5's. The kit requires the motor to have a vacuum ported Fuel Pressure Regulator, and I may be wrong but the stock motors do not have these.<BR>My bottle is in the trunk.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000008||NOS3800||07-16-2001||06:23 PM||||Another question. At the end of the day when all the racing and kicking rice ass, when I get home and turn the bottle off, there is still NOS in the line from the bottle to the Solenoid. Zex says to clear the line by unbottling it, but thats a pain. Is it safe to just turn the ignition on (not running) and turn the system on and hit the microswitch to clear te line? Mine is a dry kit. Or is it ok just to leave the NOS in the line?<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000009||baldlobo||07-16-2001||06:28 PM||||don't you have a purge silinode?(SP?), if not get one.(hell of alot easier to clear the line.) <p>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||ferrari_momo||07-16-2001||11:43 PM||||i think i gotta have NOS on my 3.4 car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  can i have turbo and NOS set up at the same time?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  going to get design1 turbo one day.  the people there are really cool too.<BR>pat k.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000011||1FST2M6||07-17-2001||08:48 AM||||uuum if you hit the switch with the car off and  have to turn the radio on if you turn the ign. to far your ign. system will spark and can cause a backfire. nothing really bad but REALLLLY D@MN loud. uum with your car running pull over and close the bottle. with the system still armed and using it like normal it'll last about 1 second. on a  wet kit just leave the nitrous in the line.. if you run a wet kit with the bottle off you'll bog the crap out of and people will stare. it's really not a big deal with the line pressureized. or if you have a purge kit just hold the button till it stops blowing. ZEX will work on a stock 2.8.. the FPR is under the pelenum and is just like nearly every other engine. just more of a pain to get too... you'll have to fight this same location issue with every dry kit. if your spraying through a turbo or s/c you have to have a dry kit. if you run wet it'll seperate and puddle in the intake the fuel once it's compressed will "fall out" or you can put a fogger nozzle in each intake runner and have equally metered and just as mean.. but cost a bit more. ||||reg||1
